  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: all incidents reported to the regulator within 24 hours, customers notified within 72 hours, and reporting required while the cause is under investigation. S2 sets 55 °C testing and a 5% failure-rate threshold, but exceeding it triggers only retesting and a corrective-action plan, not a sales stop, while per-model numeric results go to customers but not the public. S3 requires new-unit shut-off from adoption and a 6-year retrofit deadline. S4 requires built-in fire suppression at 36 months. S5 has an 8/100k review trigger, but recall is discretionary and corrective action can replace recall indefinitely; customer notices are only 'promptly'."
